Print the first swap records (sweetfb_swaplog=N) to find out why the panel
stays black.

present() copies a layer only when the swap record has its mask bit set and a
non-zero surface id, so a black panel means either no layer/surface was bound
or the bound surface is black.  sweetfb_swaplog=N prints mask + per-layer
surface ids for the first N swaps, briefly lifting the console mute so the line
is visible under sweetfb_noconsole=1.

Base: iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp from CI main (0046/0109), saved as
tmp/SweetFramebuffer_after_0124.cpp.  Only that file changes.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -387,6 +387,37 @@
 {
 	uint32_t mask = get32(rec, 0x104);
 
